  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You can tip the balance between life and death, gaining the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Pull of Death.</strong> Once per turn, when you deal damage to a creature that is missing any Hit Points with a spell or an attack roll, it takes an extra 1d4 Necrotic damage, which increases to 1d6 at Cleric level 11.</p><p><strong>Return to Life.</strong> You can cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSparetheDy]{Spare the Dying} as a Bonus Action. In addition, when you would roll dice to restore Hit Points to a creature at 0 Hit Points with a spell or Channel Divinity, you use the highest number possible for each die instead of rolling (for example, 8 Hit Points instead of 2d4).</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
